---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/it/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"devices\", \"--help\"])"
---
List, rename or revoke the devices a running daemon has granted

Usage: sluice devices [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list    The devices the daemon has granted, with their labels and pairing times
  rename  Change one device's label and nothing else
  revoke  Remove a device's grant and close its connections
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
